  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5161",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to HT through a series of biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N interacts with Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and this compound further targets HT. Similarly, Mollicellin N also interacts with A704, which is a target of the same compound, and this same compound targets HT. Additionally, Mollicellin N interacts with P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a different compound that also targets HT. These findings indicate that Mollicellin N may act through multiple distinct pathways, each involving a different target compound that ultimately leads to the same final target, HT. The integration of these pathways suggests that Mollicellin N may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially influencing cellular processes that ultimately contribute to the action of HT.",
